      "id": "savtrrz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Importance of Agriculture in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Agriculture is a vital sector of the Indian economy, supporting over half of the country's livelihood.",
        "India has three primary cropping seasons: Kharif (monsoon), Rabi (winter), and Zaid (summer).",
        "Rice and wheat dominate major food crop production, while cotton, sugarcane, and tea serve as leading cash crops.",
        "The Green Revolution revolutionized agricultural productivity through High-Yielding Variety (HYV) seeds, fertilizers, and improved irrigation.",
        "Key government initiatives include PM-KISAN, PMFBY, Soil Health Card, and e-NAM for agricultural reform."
      ],
      "id": "39es1ra"
    },
