      "content": "9. Government Initiatives"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Kharif crops (e.g., Rice, Cotton, Maize) require high rainfall and warm temperatures, sown in June-July.",
        "Rabi crops (e.g., Wheat, Mustard, Gram) are winter crops sown in October-December and harvested in spring.",
        "Dr. M.S. Swaminathan is recognized as the Father of the Green Revolution in India.",
        "PM-KISAN provides direct income transfer of ₹6,000 per annum to eligible landholding farmers."
      ],
      "id": "kk75hj8"
